-## Entry and composition
+`public/index.php -> bootstrap.php -> DirectoryComposition -> RequestBoundary -> Application -> Router -> explicit Routes/HealthRoutes/UserRoutes`. Bootstrap constructs one connection, distinct budget/trace, deny-all authentication, named tenant/action policies and one sink. The coordinator owns response selection and one summary; the front controller separately emits. The installed Alpha 7 starter's pre-coordinator failure boundary is not claimed here.
 
-- Front controller: `public/index.php`
-- Composition root: `bootstrap.php`
-- Root route manifest: `src/Routes.php`
-- Application source root: `src/`
+Feature-first source: shared account values/policy interfaces in `src/Accounts`, shared positive `UserId` in `src/Users`, operation-specific `CreateUser` and `ListUsers` directories. Routes use the narrow `positive-int` representation; the adapter immediately wraps `account_id` in `AccountId`. Identifiers use validated private constructors and `fromInteger/toInteger`, with no actor/user equivalence. Nothing discovers classes or routes.
 
-## Dependency direction
+Create's action-specific adapter runs authenticate, resolve tenant, authorize, media check, typed command parsing, then its concrete transaction handler. This handler is the single SQL owner for the independently meaningful three-write transaction. List's adapter follows the same policy order before its page parser and one-statement handler. Policies are separate constructor dependencies and replaceable without framework edits.
 
-This diagram records construction and dependency ownership, not request-time control flow.
+Create accepts exact `application/json` and at most 1024 bytes/depth 8. Exact fields `id:int`, `name:string`, `email:string` all pass shape/type validation before values. Positive IDs are client-selected; names are 1–80 UTF-8 bytes with no ASCII controls or trim padding; email is <=254 bytes and an unchanged PHP FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL result. No normalization; duplicate JSON keys retain PHP's last-value limitation. Shape/type failure is generic 400; unacceptable value 422; body overflow 413; media 415. Named conflict is 409. Validation occurs before protected SQL. Success is 201 with exact `data:{id,name,email}`. See data for transactional semantics.
 
-```text
-public/index.php
-├── requires bootstrap.php -> TerminalRequestCoordinator
-│   ├── RequestBoundary -> Application -> Router
-│   │   └── Routes -> HealthRoutes -> dependency-free HealthHandler
-│   ├── UnknownFailureBoundary
-│   ├── CorrelationId
-│   └── RequestSummarySink
-└── constructs ResponseEmitter
-```
+List accepts only optional canonical positive decimal `after_user_id` within PHP_INT_MAX. Missing means first page; null, empty, arrays, unknown keys, leading zeroes and overflow fail 400 before protected SQL. One query fetches <=21, immediate `UserSummary` projection validates every row, and I/O-free mapping emits <=20 with `next_after_user_id` set only when lookahead exists. SQLite returns native integer IDs; strings are rejected. Ordering is ascending ID, static-fixture keyset pagination, no concurrent snapshot guarantee.
 
-Dependencies may point only in the direction shown above. Record a deliberate exception in `docs/decisions/` before implementation.
+Health/404/405 retain explicit no-store. Protected responses and shared mapped 400/413 responses use private no-store (deliberate stronger cache restriction than the starter). Unknown failures remain generic private no-store. Summary ownership is `.ai/observability.md`; configuration is `.ai/configuration.md`.
 
